The io.EOF loop idiom: "if err == io.EOF { break }" then "return n, nil"; other
errors are wrapped with "source: line %d: %w". A sentinel io.EOF must NOT be in the
set. What remains is bufio's Unresolved(memory) field load under the fmt.Errorf
wrap, marked "possibly handled" by the comparison with io.EOF (unresolved value).
